From: Ethan Hill <ethan.hill1999@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:16:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] CandyOS P28: QS footer actions flat-donor strip

- 28.6.1 qs_footer_actions_background: flat #ff161616, square top
  corners. The donor 4.4 shade band (status_bar_expanded_header,
  notification_header_bg = flat opaque #FF000000, donor
  values/colors.xml) was a full-bleed square-cornered band riding the
  panel from the first frame. Stock AOSP kept the footer actions strip
  on the M3 "underSurface" layer (material_dynamic_neutral0 = pure
  black) with rounded top corners, 4dp elevation and a fade confined
  to the last 10% of the QS expansion (FooterActionsViewModel alpha
  delay 0.9) - which the P24 flat #ff161616 shade panel turned into a
  black band popping in over the page (user 28.3 emulator-pass
  critique: reads as a bug). Flatten to the P3 palette so the strip
  reads seamless with the shade panel behind it (same ruling as the
  P24 header strip, kitkat_shade_header_bg); the keyguard QS gets the
  same flat band, matching its #ff161616 tiles.
- 28.6.2 footer_actions: outlineProvider=none. The strip is a flat
  band of the panel now, so it must not cast the stock 4dp elevation
  shadow onto the page; the elevation itself stays matched to the QS
  scroll view for z-order parity (the footer keeps drawing above the
  QS content during the expansion animation).

The stock last-10% fade is kept on purpose: with band color == panel
color the surface transition is invisible - only the glyphs ride the
fade, same as the header contents do.

Change-Id: Ib9072564fdf9ffe12526bd61cda3d5870db9d486
---
 .../res-keyguard/layout/footer_actions.xml    |  7 +++++++
 .../drawable/qs_footer_actions_background.xml | 20 ++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/res-keyguard/layout/footer_actions.xml b/packages/SystemUI/res-keyguard/layout/footer_actions.xml
index 4a2a1cb9dc6d..6395e1bfd8cd 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/res-keyguard/layout/footer_actions.xml
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/res-keyguard/layout/footer_actions.xml
@@ -16,11 +16,18 @@
 -->
 
 <!-- Action buttons for footer in QS/QQS, containing settings button, power off button etc -->
+<!-- KitKat UI Project (P28.6): the strip is a flat band of the shade
+     panel now (see qs_footer_actions_background), so it must not cast
+     the stock 4dp elevation shadow onto the page. outlineProvider=none
+     kills the shadow while the elevation itself stays matched to the
+     QS scroll view (z-order parity: the footer keeps drawing above the
+     QS content during the expansion animation). -->
 <LinearLayout
     xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
     android:layout_width="match_parent"
     android:layout_height="@dimen/footer_actions_height"
     android:elevation="@dimen/qs_panel_elevation"
+    android:outlineProvider="none"
     android:paddingTop="@dimen/qs_footer_actions_top_padding"
     android:paddingBottom="@dimen/qs_footer_actions_bottom_padding"
     android:background="@drawable/qs_footer_actions_background"
diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/res/drawable/qs_footer_actions_background.xml b/packages/SystemUI/res/drawable/qs_footer_actions_background.xml
index a7e8762a2593..7e4fcd92b09f 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/res/drawable/qs_footer_actions_background.xml
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/res/drawable/qs_footer_actions_background.xml
@@ -13,10 +13,24 @@
      See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
      limitations under the License.
 -->
+<!-- KitKat UI Project (P28.6): donor 4.4 shade band treatment for the
+     QS footer actions strip (settings/power/user row). The donor band
+     (status_bar_expanded_header, notification_header_bg = flat opaque
+     #FF000000) was a FLAT, full-bleed, square-cornered surface riding
+     the panel from the first frame - no rounded corners, no elevation
+     shadow. Stock AOSP kept this strip on the M3 "underSurface" layer
+     (material_dynamic_neutral0 = pure black) with rounded top corners
+     and 4dp elevation, fading in over only the last 10% of the QS
+     expansion - which the P24 flat #ff161616 shade panel turned into a
+     black band that pops in over the page. Flatten to the P3 palette
+     so the strip reads seamless with the shade panel behind it (same
+     ruling as the P24 header strip, kitkat_shade_header_bg); the
+     keyguard QS gets the same flat band, matching its #ff161616
+     tiles. -->
 <inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
     <shape>
-        <solid android:color="?attr/underSurface"/>
-        <corners android:topLeftRadius="@dimen/qs_corner_radius"
-                 android:topRightRadius="@dimen/qs_corner_radius"/>
+        <solid android:color="#ff161616"/>
+        <corners android:topLeftRadius="0dp"
+                 android:topRightRadius="0dp"/>
     </shape>
 </inset>
